'''''Hygroamblystegium varium''''' is a species of [[moss]] in the [[Amblystegiaceae]] family.<ref name="GBIF">{{GBIF |id=7742683|taxon=''Hygroamblystegium varium'' |accessdate=21 October 2022}}</ref> It has a [[cosmopolitan distribution]].<ref name="GBIF"/>

''Hygroamblystegium varium'' is known to be able to use [[artificial light]] to grow in places which are otherwise devoid of natural light, such as [[Niagara Cave]].
<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Thatcher |first1=Edward P. |title=Observations on Bryophytes Living in an Artificially Illuminated Limestone Cave |journal=The American Midland Naturalist |date=1947 |volume=37 |issue=3 |pages=797–800 |doi=10.2307/2421476 |jstor=2421476 }}</ref>

